# SRG-APP-000170-AU-002530  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to require the change of at
# least eight of the total number of characters when passwords are changed.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000170-AU-002530
group:           V-206473
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004066
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    The product's nearest capability is password history
                 (enablePasswordHistory with passwordHistoryCount), which blocks reuse of a
                 stored previous password in full but does not measure how many characters
                 changed, so the application cannot enforce the eight-character difference
                 itself.

external:        An external authentication provider selected through authentication.conf
                 authType (LDAP, SAML or Scripted), whose own password policy engine can
                 enforce a minimum number of changed characters
external:        The organization's password management procedure for the native emergency
                 account of last resort
external:        Operating system password policy for host accounts

manual_reason:   Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 exposes no setting that measures how many
                 characters of a new password differ from the previous one. The native
                 password controls in authentication.conf.spec:437-568 are minimum length,
                 the four character-class minimums, expiry and alerting, lockout, and
                 password history with a stored count; none of them expresses a
                 per-character change threshold, so no configuration value can decide this
                 requirement and writing a condition over a substitute setting would report
                 a finding for something the product has no control over.

citation:        SRG-APP-000170-AU-002530 check text; authentication.conf.spec:437-568 (the
                 complete set of [splunk_auth] password controls: minPasswordLength,
                 minPasswordUppercase, minPasswordLowercase, minPasswordDigit,
                 minPasswordSpecial, expirePasswordDays, expireAlertDays,
                 expireUserAccounts, forceWeakPasswordChange, lockout settings,
                 enablePasswordHistory at 554-560 and passwordHistoryCount at 561-568)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 provides
                 no setting that requires a minimum number of characters to change when a
                 password is changed, and the requirement is carried by the external
                 authentication provider or by organizational password procedure.
